THE TEXT IN THIS FOLDER — not the site's code (docs/history/513). Written by tools/writings-more.py.
Every text here is public domain, or openly licensed and credited on every card. Nothing of uncertain status is included.

apocrypha/     Apocrypha, King James Version (1611; the standard text of 1769), from eBible.org's eng-kjv_vpl
               (https://ebible.org/Scriptures/eng-kjv_vpl.zip): "Public Domain". In the UK the KJV's printing is under the
               Crown's letters patent, as is the KJV the site already shows (data/bible); that patent governs printing, and
               the text is otherwise public domain. Tobit, Judith, Additions to Esther, Wisdom, Sirach, Baruch, the Letter of
               Jeremiah (the KJV's Baruch 6), Prayer of Azariah, Susanna, Bel and the Dragon, 1–2 Maccabees, 1–2 Esdras,
               Prayer of Manasseh.
enoch/         R. H. Charles, The Book of Enoch (SPCK, 1917). Public domain (Charles died 1931). Transcription: Project
               Gutenberg #77935 (https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/77935); headings, the editors' notes and the
               transcribers' marks left out, Charles's brackets kept. Where Charles prints the Greek beside the Ethiopic,
               the Greek follows on the same card after "Greek:".
jubilees/      R. H. Charles, The Book of Jubilees (SPCK, 1917). Public domain. As exported by Sefaria
               (https://github.com/Sefaria/Sefaria-Export), version marked "Public Domain".
josephus/      William Whiston's translation of Josephus (1737). Public domain (Whiston died 1752). Antiquities, The
               Jewish War and Against Apion as exported by Sefaria: The Jewish War marked "Public Domain"; Antiquities and
               Against Apion are Wikisource's transcriptions, marked CC BY-SA (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/),
               shared here under the same licence with this credit. Whiston's footnotes left out. The Life: Project
               Gutenberg #2846 (https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2846), public domain.
mishnah/       The Mishnah, ed. Romm, Vilna 1913 (National Library of Israel), digitised by Sefaria and marked "Public
               Domain" in every one of its 63 tractates' files. Markup removed.
mishnah-en/    D. A. de Sola and M. J. Raphall, Eighteen Treatises from the Mishna (1843), via Sefaria, marked "Public
               Domain". Only chapters whose mishnayot are numbered as the Vilna text's are included; the note numbers are
               removed. Not included: Charles Taylor's Pirqe Aboth (1897), which Sefaria marks "unknown"; every other English.
fathers-grc/   Kirsopp Lake's Greek text, The Apostolic Fathers (Loeb, 1912–13): public domain (Lake died 1946).
               Transcription: First1KGreek, Open Greek and Latin (https://github.com/OpenGreekAndLatin/First1KGreek),
               CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/); this folder's Greek is shared under the same
               licence with this credit. Apparatus notes left out. Where Lake prints only the Latin (Polycarp 10–12, the
               end of Hermas) the transcription spells it in Greek letters; those passages are left out.
fathers-en/    J. B. Lightfoot and J. R. Harmer, The Apostolic Fathers (1891), as the Christian Classics Ethereal Library
               prints it (https://www.ccel.org/ccel/lightfoot/fathers.xml). Public domain (Lightfoot died 1889, Harmer 1944).
justin-en/     Ante-Nicene Fathers I, ed. A. Roberts, J. Donaldson, A. C. Coxe (1885): Justin's First and Second Apology
               and Dialogue with Trypho (tr. M. Dods, G. Reith, B. P. Pratten). Public domain. Via CCEL
               (https://www.ccel.org/ccel/schaff/anf01.xml); the editors' notes left out.
justin-grc/    Gerhard Rauschen's Greek text of the First Apology (Bonn, 1911): public domain (Rauschen died 1917).
               Transcription: First1KGreek, CC BY-SA 4.0, as above.
confessions/   E. B. Pusey's translation of Augustine's Confessions (1838). Public domain (Pusey died 1882). Via CCEL
               (https://www.ccel.org/ccel/augustine/confess.xml).
gilgamesh/     M. Jastrow and A. T. Clay, An Old Babylonian Version of the Gilgamesh Epic (Yale, 1920): the Pennsylvania
               and Yale tablets, a card a column. Public domain (Jastrow died 1921, Clay 1925). Project Gutenberg #11000
               (https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/11000); note numbers removed, line breaks shown as " / ".
zohar/         Zohar Chadash ("Zohar Chadash", Torat Emet) and Tikkunei Zohar ("Tikkunei Zohar - Vocalized", Torat Emet),
               the Aramaic as exported by Sefaria, each marked "Public Domain". A card a paragraph, under its parasha or
               its daf (Sefaria's numbering). Not included: the Zohar itself — every Aramaic version in the export
               (Sulam Edition 1945, Vocalized Zohar 2013, the Hebrew translation) is marked licence "unknown"; Tikkunei
               Zohar "Constantinople, 1740" is CC BY-NC; every English (Soncino 1931-34 and Pritzker are in copyright).

The Project Gutenberg files are used as public-domain text with Project Gutenberg's own header, licence and
trademark removed, as its licence allows.
